https://github.com/microsoft/MoGe

The upstream ViT-B model is released under the MIT license. The repository
also retains Apache License 2.0 notices for incorporated DINOv2 code.
The accompanying MoGe-LICENSE.txt preserves both upstream license texts.

This application adapts the original ONNX export for relative-depth effects:
unused normals and metric-scale branches are removed, the token count is
derived from input dimensions, and point-map Z is shifted positive. The
original sigmoid validity mask is retained. Retained neural weights and
computation are converted to FP16. Positional cubic interpolation uses
equivalent separable matrices for DirectML. This output is relative depth,
not metric distance.


